  hsa:condition <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/condition/general> ;
  skos:definition "Take a warm bath or shower 60–90 minutes before bedtime for optimal results. Keep it lukewarm rather than too hot, and allow time for your body to cool down naturally."@en ;
  skos:editorialNote "Wiki scores ease 3 on the item page but 5 in both summary tables. Write-up has no citations."@en .

<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/try-pink-noise> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Pink noise is popular, but the evidence is weak, and one trial found it reduced dream (REM) sleep."@en ;
  hsa:kind "advice" ;
  skos:notation "1.4.2" ;
  skos:altLabel "Try pink noise instead of white noise"@en ;
  skos:broader <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/mask-noise-with-steady-sound> ;
  hsa:mechanism <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/sleep-environment> ;
  hsa:timeOfDay <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/timeOfDay/during-the-night> ;
  hsa:condition <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/condition/general> ;
  skos:definition "Use free apps or YouTube to find pink noise sounds, or try a white noise machine with a pink noise setting. Experiment with different soundscapes to find what works best for you."@en ;
  skos:editorialNote "Wiki's own scores disagree sharply on evidence (item page: 'well supported'; classification table: 'weak evidence', impact 1). Write-up has no citations. Plain line corrected after the literature search: Basner 2026 RCT found all-night pink noise cut REM sleep; earplugs blocked traffic noise."@en .

<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/wear-socks-to-bed> a skos:Concept ;
