  skos:definition "Use blue light filter apps on screens, wear blue light-blocking glasses, and switch to warm, dim lighting (like red or amber bulbs) 1–2 hours before bed."@en ;
  skos:editorialNote "Wiki item says 'reduce blue light'. The NSF 2024 consensus did not reach consensus that pre-bedtime screen light impairs sleep; the plain line is about room light overall, not screen filters. Write-up has no citations."@en .

