<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/naps-and-night-sleep> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Short naps are fine for most people; long or late naps can make night sleep harder."@en ;
  hsa:kind "advice" ;
  skos:notation "3.2.1" ;
  skos:altLabel "Naps harm nighttime sleep"@en ;
  hsa:deprecated true ;
  dct:isReplacedBy <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/keep-naps-short-and-early> ;
  skos:definition "If you nap, keep it under 30 minutes and avoid napping after 3 PM to minimize its impact on nighttime sleep."@en ;
  skos:editorialNote "Merged into keep-naps-short-and-early: Wiki 3.2.1 is the claim behind 1.1.4, and its own tip is the same advice. Earlier note: The wiki item is a claim ('Naps harm nighttime sleep'), not advice, and its own evidence says it depends. Recommend merging into 1.1.4 and moving the claim to the myths list."@en .

<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/bed-is-for-sleep> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Use your bed only for sleep and sex."@en ;
  hsa:kind "advice" ;
  skos:notation "3.2.2" ;
  skos:altLabel "Use the bed only for sleep and intimacy"@en ;
  skos:broader <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/stimulus-control> ;
  skos:closeMatch <https://iha-health-glossary.pages.dev/terms/slp-reconditioning-therapy/> ;
  hsa:mechanism <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/learned-association> ;
  hsa:timeOfDay <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/timeOfDay/any-time> ;
  hsa:condition <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/condition/insomnia> ;
  hsa:problem <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/problem/technology> ;
  hsa:problem <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/problem/evening-phone> ;
  hsa:problem <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/problem/bedroom-devices> ;
  skos:definition "If you can’t sleep after 20 minutes, get out of bed and do a relaxing activity (e.g., reading under dim light) until you feel sleepy, then return to bed."@en ;
  skos:editorialNote "Part of stimulus control (NHLBI calls it reconditioning therapy). Wiki tip folds in 3.2.3."@en .

<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/get-up-if-you-cant-sleep> a skos:Concept ;
